                <pb facs="0265" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Gibraltar</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Williams</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gibraltar</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-16T10:00:00+00:00">March 16, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 16—7:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following information was given British Intelligence Service by an Englishman
                    who had deserted Spanish Government forces and who came to Gibraltar a few days
                    ago from Castellon.</p>
                <p>On February 18th an American battalion 450 strong arrived near Chinchon between
                    Madrid and Valencia. Said to be fully armed and equipped. He added that he had
                    been wounded, and cared for at an American dressing station February 23rd 50
                    kilometres behind the lines.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
